Z||000000||FieroBUZZ||08-31-2001||10:21 PM||||Long ago you could buy a kit to power crank windows.  The motor was enclosed in a small box which mounted over the splines on the shaft (inside the interior but not in the door).  Used to be in the van and hot rod mags.  Anyone know if they are still available?   TIA<P>Gary<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||08-31-2001||11:43 PM||||if anyone has it, it's J.C. whitless.... I always thought that system looked like crap. worse in Fiero it puts a large protrusion right were most people rest their leg against the door while driving. (The window crank hitting me in the knee was one of the reasons I converted mine... I can't imagine having a motor box there.)<P>Is not that difficult to convert to OE power hardware. Time consuming more than anything. One story is in my cave but there are several others online.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-31-2001).]||||reg||1
